Subject: [PATCH] firmware_class: look where Android keeps firmware

The kernel reads firmware straight from /lib/firmware, which Android does not
have, so every file has to be asked of ueventd with a uevent. On the 3.10
kernel that kept the tablet from suspending: at each suspend the kernel caches
again all the firmware it has handed out, and a process woken by the uevents
(the health HAL) aborted the freeze each time (../kernel/patches/0022).

The files are in /vendor/firmware or /system/etc/firmware, the modem's on the
firmware partition, mounted at /firmware.
---
--- drivers/base/firmware_class.c
+++ drivers/base/firmware_class.c
@@ -297,7 +297,11 @@
 	"/lib/firmware/updates/" UTS_RELEASE,
 	"/lib/firmware/updates",
 	"/lib/firmware/" UTS_RELEASE,
-	"/lib/firmware"
+	"/lib/firmware",
+	/* Android's, where the files are; /lib is not there at all. */
+	"/vendor/firmware",
+	"/system/etc/firmware",
+	"/firmware/image"
 };
 
